# apps/sales-web: the CRM's frontend.
# The server-side calls go straight to the apps' ports, not through the dev
# proxy of `dafne dev` (https://<app>.dafne.localhost).
# The CRM's API (server-side calls: backendFetch).
BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
# apps/auth: /api/auth is proxied there (next.config.ts), sessions and users.
AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3001
# This app's public URL (Origin of the server-side calls): one of apps/auth's
# AUTH_ALLOWED_HOSTS (or TRUSTED_ORIGINS). `pnpm dafne dev` serves it.
APP_URL=https://sales-web.dafne.localhost

## Logs (@dafne/frontend-logger)
# Lowest level of the server's lines (debug | info | warn | error; default
# debug, info in production) and of the browser's (NEXT_PUBLIC_LOG_LEVEL).
LOG_LEVEL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_LOG_LEVEL=

## Observability (docs/observability.md)
# The Next server's traces, metrics and logs over OTLP (instrumentation.ts):
# the otel service of compose.yaml in development, opt-in: uncomment both
# below, and run `pnpm dafne dev --telemetry`. Empty: none, logs on stdout only.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel.dafne.localhost:4318
# Where the browser's telemetry (Grafana Faro) goes, through /telemetry on
# this app (next.config.ts): the alloy service of compose.yaml in development,
# Grafana Cloud's Faro collector URL in production. Read when the app is
# built. Empty: no browser telemetry.
# FARO_URL=http://faro.dafne.localhost:12347/collect
# Share of browser sessions sent, 0 to 1 (default 1).
FARO_SAMPLE_RATE=1
